{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>Elohim</b> — Some say: כי צדיק פועל גם ישפוט אשר יזעום ה' בכל יום (for the righteous one acts and also judges, whom YHWH is angry at every day), and the meaning is 'judges always.' In my opinion: כי צדיק (for [he is] righteous) is an epithet for 'judge.'" "<b>ואל זועם</b> (and El is angry) — the phrase <b>בכל יום</b> (every day) connects with the verse after it, <b>אם לא ישוב</b> (if he does not return), and the word אשר is omitted, like להתחזק עם לבבם שלם, as if it were <b>ואם לא ישוב</b> (and if he does not return) אשר <b>חרבו ילטוש</b> (whose sword he sharpens). Some say: <b>כי אל</b> (for El) — like אלה (these), in the manner of: אל נולדו להרפא." "And the word <b>אל</b> refers back to the word <b>רשעים</b> (wicked) that is above."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {1 "The two scriptural citations (להתחזק עם לבבם שלם and אל נולדו להרפא) could not be identified; rendered hyper-literally as they stand."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:26:34.643607128Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}